{
  "id": "kampung",
  "name": "The Kampung Quarter",
  "notes": [
    "COMPOSITION. A village clearing ringed by houses, closed at the back by a",
    "wall of jungle and opened at the front by the river. The eye enters on the",
    "path at the top, is stopped by the shade tree and the well at the centre of",
    "the common, and is then handed left to the water and the beached perahu.",
    "",
    "SCALE IS THE POINT HERE. The shipping kampung plate draws stilt houses the",
    "height of the player. These are 100px to the ridge against a 32px player —",
    "26px of pile, 36 of wall, 34 of roof — with a metre of eave overhang and a",
    "black void underneath, which is the single strongest cue that the house is",
    "lifted off the ground.",
    "",
    "DEPTH PLANES. 1) two hazed layers of canopy with palm crowns breaking the",
    "skyline. 2) the four houses of the back row, the surau, the common. 3) the",
    "two near houses and the palm cluster at the bottom corners, emitted as",
    "walk-behind overlays.",
    "",
    "CULTURE MARKERS: attap roofs with crossed bargeboards, the surau and its",
    "finial, kain and sarong on the bamboo drying racks, the rice mortar, the",
    "perahu on the bank."
  ],
